Relevant columns & how they will be used  
• `year`, `month`, `day`      : build a calendar `DATE` so we can aggregate “daily”.  
• `latitude`, `longitude`    : keep the coordinates that will be reported with each daily‑average value.  
• `wind_speed`                : numeric value to average. Stored in tenths of m s‑1, so divide by 10.  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX`            : wildcard helper that tells us which yearly table we are reading; lets us choose only the 2005‑2015 tables.  

Main conditions  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '2005' AND '2015'` (or an explicit list of those 11 tables)  
• `wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)` – drop the missing / NaN values.  
• `year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015` – safeguard in case any record is mis‑filed in the wrong table.  

Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complex BigQuery queries (each limited to 20 rows except the final answer) that progressively check the data and finally return the requested result.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a few rows from one year (2008) to see the wind‑speed values.
SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2008`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List distinct years found in the 2005‑2015 range across all tables.
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '2005' AND '2015'
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Compute one day’s average wind speed (arbitrarily 2005‑01‑15) to verify conversion /10.
SELECT DATE(year,month,day) AS obs_date,
       AVG(wind_speed/10.0) AS avg_wind_ms
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2005`
WHERE year=2005 AND month=1 AND day=15
      AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
GROUP BY obs_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Union two tables (2005 & 2006) and show a few rows after converting wind speed.
SELECT DATE(year,month,day) AS obs_date,
       latitude, longitude,
       wind_speed/10.0 AS wind_ms
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2005`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
UNION ALL
SELECT DATE(year,month,day), latitude, longitude, wind_speed/10.0
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2006`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Daily average wind speed per coordinate for one year (2007) – quick sanity check.
SELECT DATE(year,month,day)         AS obs_date,
       latitude, longitude,
       AVG(wind_speed/10.0)         AS avg_wind_ms
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2007`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
GROUP BY obs_date, latitude, longitude
ORDER BY avg_wind_ms DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Same as #5 but using wildcard tables for 2005‑2006 only, via _TABLE_SUFFIX.
SELECT DATE(year,month,day) AS obs_date,
       latitude, longitude,
       AVG(wind_speed/10.0) AS avg_wind_ms
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX IN ('2005','2006')
      AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
GROUP BY obs_date, latitude, longitude
ORDER BY avg_wind_ms DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Top 5 daily averages in 2005 only.
WITH dailies AS (
  SELECT DATE(year,month,day) AS obs_date,
         latitude, longitude,
         AVG(wind_speed/10.0) AS avg_wind_ms
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2005`
  WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
  GROUP BY obs_date, latitude, longitude
)
SELECT *
FROM dailies
ORDER BY avg_wind_ms DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Top 5 daily averages across 2005‑2008 using UNION ALL (explicit list).
WITH base AS (
  SELECT year,month,day,latitude,longitude,wind_speed FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2005`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year,month,day,latitude,longitude,wind_speed FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2006`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year,month,day,latitude,longitude,wind_speed FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2007`
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year,month,day,latitude,longitude,wind_speed FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2008`
)
SELECT DATE(year,month,day) AS obs_date,
       latitude, longitude,
       AVG(wind_speed/10.0) AS avg_wind_ms
FROM base
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
GROUP BY obs_date, latitude, longitude
ORDER BY avg_wind_ms DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as #8 but using one wildcard scan (faster, less typing).
WITH core AS (
  SELECT DATE(year,month,day) AS obs_date,
         latitude, longitude,
         wind_speed/10.0        AS wind_ms
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '2005' AND '2008'
        AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
)
SELECT obs_date, latitude, longitude,
       AVG(wind_ms) AS avg_wind_ms
FROM core
GROUP BY obs_date, latitude, longitude
ORDER BY avg_wind_ms DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL ANSWER – Top 5 (2005‑2015) daily‑average wind speeds with their date & coordinates.
WITH core AS (
  SELECT 
    DATE(year, month, day)                 AS obs_date,
    latitude,
    longitude,
    wind_speed / 10.0                      AS wind_ms
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '2005' AND '2015'
        AND year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015
        AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL
        AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
), daily AS (
  SELECT
    obs_date,
    latitude,
    longitude,
    AVG(wind_ms) AS avg_wind_ms
  FROM core
  GROUP BY obs_date, latitude, longitude
)
SELECT 
  obs_date,
  latitude,
  longitude,
  avg_wind_ms
FROM daily
ORDER BY avg_wind_ms DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

